 they're much  better I mean when we used to talk about  the hotlines they weren't hotlines at  all in Hollywood it's a telephone that  they pick up and talk to they wasn't  like that it was a teleprinter that took  hours to go backwards and forwards it  was it was astonishingly cruel Doctor  Strange Love was right absolutely the  more I see doctor Strangelove the more  puff from the very end where Slim  Pickens goes down on the nuclear that's  the only bit that's surreal the rest of  it believe me there is something in our  nuclear history where I can tick off yes  that's happened that's happened that's  happened and that's happened It's a  Wonderful film Kubrick's Great  Masterpiece Dr Strangler it gets less  surreal the more you the more you watch  it however deterrence is is about this  this ability to respond and and yet we  have that ability  um whether it's a safe thing to do who  knows but I have to say let's not forget  that Millie the American uh chairman of  the Joint Chiefs was in touch with  grazimov uh sorry with the uh uh you  know gorasimov this week and Lloyd  Austin the defense Chief was in touch  with shogu this week so the Americans  and the Russians are at the top level  they're phoning each other and talking  to each other in order to keep the  temperature as low as they can as  military professionals Michael  informative as ever if not more so thank  you very much indeed Michael Clark there  and you've been watching a question and  answer program on Sky News tonight about  the war in Ukraine and uh coming up on  Sky News at eight o'clock  foreign  [Music]


